  "details": "<p>Epigraphic evidence indicates that the temple's patrons in the late second century B.C. are Marcus Calvius Publius, son of Publius, and Caius Geminius Mateiclus, son of Caius. Their names are recorded on a epistyle block as part of a dedicatory inscription.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "The Temple of Castor and Pollux at Cora was originally built between the fourth and the second centuries B.C. The partially extant architrave carries an inscription of the first century B.C.",
